      "causeSummary": "The Utilities division's machine hours are 6,400, which already includes the Concrete division's 2,800 yard hours, so those hours are counted twice. Because the rate of 40.00 stays fixed, the four divisional shares now foot to 752,000 against a pool of only 640,000, and the paper over-allocates the pool by 112,000. The re-derived rate check falls to 34.04, therefore the schedule cannot be signed until the driver is de-duplicated.",
